cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these tables, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "Surface entropy budget of BR-Npw (northern Pantanal): code and derived tables"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/sanxin90-sys/entropy-paper"
authors:
  - alias: "sanxin90-sys"
abstract: >-
  Python pipeline and derived tables for the surface entropy budget of the
  AmeriFlux site BR-Npw (northern Pantanal, Brazil) from the ONEFlux
  half-hourly product for 2015-2016, with the Planck (4/3) convention for
  the radiation terms, closure scenarios S0-S3, a daily block bootstrap and
  one-at-a-time sensitivity analysis. AmeriFlux input data are not included.
keywords:
  - entropy production
  - radiation entropy
  - eddy covariance
  - energy-balance closure
  - Pantanal
  - FLUXNET
